# Data and State

- PostgreSQL is the durable source of truth for core business/session metadata.
- Redis/Valkey may be used for cache, rate limits, short locks and transient coordination, not as the only durable truth.
- Provisioning requests create durable session/job identities and complete asynchronously.
- Use explicit events for important state changes where useful.
- Keep operational telemetry distinct from learner activity telemetry.
- Do not centrally record complete user shell history by default without a defined requirement and policy.
- Schema migrations require rollback/recovery thinking.
- Backup and restore behavior must follow the canonical recovery policy before production.
